  "problems": [
    {
      "problem_id": "demo-b-s02-p01",
      "topic": "Solving a linear equation with variables on both sides",
      "start_turn_id": "demo-b-s02-t001",
      "end_turn_id": "demo-b-s02-t048"
    }
  ],
  "turns": [
    {
      "_id": "0",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s02",
      "sequence_id": 1,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Let's look at this one: solve 5 times the quantity x minus 3 equals 2x plus 9.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s02-t001",
      "start_time": "2026-01-20T16:00:00.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-20T16:00:16.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "1",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s02",
      "sequence_id": 2,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "So we've got parentheses on one side and x's on both sides, got it.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s02-t002",
      "start_time": "2026-01-20T16:00:20.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-20T16:00:36.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "2",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s02",
      "sequence_id": 3,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Right, that's the whole problem — nothing else attached to it.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s02-t003",
      "start_time": "2026-01-20T16:00:38.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-20T16:01:38.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "3",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s02",
      "sequence_id": 4,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "So the bracket means we have to multiply the 5 through before anything else, right?",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s02-t004",
      "start_time": "2026-01-20T16:01:46.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-20T16:02:51.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "4",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s02",
      "sequence_id": 5,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Exactly, that 5 has to hit both terms inside the parentheses.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s02-t005",
      "start_time": "2026-01-20T16:02:54.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-20T16:03:56.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "5",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s02",
      "sequence_id": 6,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "So 5 times x is 5x, and 5 times negative 3 is negative 15.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s02-t006",
      "start_time": "2026-01-20T16:03:59.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-20T16:04:29.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "6",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s02",
      "sequence_id": 7,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Right, so the left side becomes 5x minus 15.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s02-t007",
      "start_time": "2026-01-20T16:04:30.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-20T16:05:21.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "7",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s02",
      "sequence_id": 8,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "And the right side just stays as 2x plus 9, since there's no bracket there.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s02-t008",
      "start_time": "2026-01-20T16:05:29.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-20T16:06:18.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "8",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s02",
      "sequence_id": 9,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "So now we've got 5x minus 15 equals 2x plus 9 — a clean equation to work with.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s02-t009",
      "start_time": "2026-01-20T16:06:25.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-20T16:07:18.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "9",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s02",
      "sequence_id": 10,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "Okay, so I'll subtract 2x from both sides now.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s02-t010",
      "start_time": "2026-01-20T16:07:23.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-20T16:08:05.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "10",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s02",
      "sequence_id": 11,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Go ahead, write out what that leaves you with.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s02-t011",
      "start_time": "2026-01-20T16:08:11.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-20T16:08:41.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "11",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s02",
      "sequence_id": 12,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "5x minus 2x is 3x, so it's 3x minus 15 equals 9.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s02-t012",
      "start_time": "2026-01-20T16:08:48.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-20T16:09:11.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "12",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s02",
      "sequence_id": 13,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Good, now what do we do with that minus 15?",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s02-t013",
      "start_time": "2026-01-20T16:09:11.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-20T16:09:23.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "13",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s02",
      "sequence_id": 14,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "Add 15 to both sides — that gives 3x equals 24.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s02-t014",
      "start_time": "2026-01-20T16:09:30.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-20T16:09:58.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "14",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s02",
      "sequence_id": 15,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Nice, and now the last step to isolate x?",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s02-t015",
      "start_time": "2026-01-20T16:10:05.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-20T16:10:25.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "15",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s02",
      "sequence_id": 16,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "Divide both sides by 3, so x equals 8.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s02-t016",
      "start_time": "2026-01-20T16:10:27.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-20T16:10:47.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "16",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s02",
      "sequence_id": 17,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "That's the value — let's think about whether there's another way to reach it.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s02-t017",
      "start_time": "2026-01-20T16:10:52.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-20T16:11:33.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "17",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s02",
      "sequence_id": 18,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "I guess instead of moving the 2x, we could've moved it the other way first?",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s02-t018",
      "start_time": "2026-01-20T16:11:37.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-20T16:11:57.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "18",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s02",
      "sequence_id": 19,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Sure, walk me through what that would look like.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s02-t019",
      "start_time": "2026-01-20T16:12:05.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-20T16:12:37.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "19",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s02",
      "sequence_id": 20,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "We'd subtract 5x from both sides instead, so the x terms end up on the right.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s02-t020",
      "start_time": "2026-01-20T16:12:42.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-20T16:13:40.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "20",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s02",
      "sequence_id": 21,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "And what would that leave us with on each side?",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s02-t021",
      "start_time": "2026-01-20T16:13:47.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-20T16:14:22.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "21",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s02",
      "sequence_id": 22,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "Negative 15 equals negative 3x plus 9, I think.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s02-t022",
      "start_time": "2026-01-20T16:14:23.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-20T16:14:42.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "22",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s02",
      "sequence_id": 23,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Sounds right so far — what's the next move in that version?",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s02-t023",
      "start_time": "2026-01-20T16:14:49.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-20T16:15:53.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "23",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s02",
      "sequence_id": 24,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "Let me just jot that equation down on my scratch pad before I lose it.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s02-t024",
      "start_time": "2026-01-20T16:15:58.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-20T16:16:14.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "24",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s02",
      "sequence_id": 25,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Sure, take a second to get it written down.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s02-t025",
      "start_time": "2026-01-20T16:16:20.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-20T16:17:13.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "25",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s02",
      "sequence_id": 26,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "Okay, so from there I'd subtract 9 from both sides.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s02-t026",
      "start_time": "2026-01-20T16:17:18.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-20T16:18:20.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "26",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s02",
      "sequence_id": 27,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Go on, what does that give you?",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s02-t027",
      "start_time": "2026-01-20T16:18:20.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-20T16:19:08.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "27",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s02",
      "sequence_id": 28,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "Negative 24 equals negative 3x, then divide by negative 3.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s02-t028",
      "start_time": "2026-01-20T16:19:14.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-20T16:20:12.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "28",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s02",
      "sequence_id": 29,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "And that division should land you right back at the same answer as before.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s02-t029",
      "start_time": "2026-01-20T16:20:12.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-20T16:21:07.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "29",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s02",
      "sequence_id": 30,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "Wait, could dividing negative numbers like that flip the sign somewhere and mess it up?",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s02-t030",
      "start_time": "2026-01-20T16:21:08.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-20T16:21:43.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "30",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s02",
      "sequence_id": 31,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Good instinct to check — try the division and see what actually happens to the sign.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s02-t031",
      "start_time": "2026-01-20T16:21:44.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-20T16:22:34.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "31",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s02",
      "sequence_id": 32,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "Negative 24 over negative 3 is positive 8, so the negatives cancel out fine.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s02-t032",
      "start_time": "2026-01-20T16:22:34.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-20T16:23:07.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "32",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s02",
      "sequence_id": 33,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Exactly, both routes land on the same value, just from opposite directions.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s02-t033",
      "start_time": "2026-01-20T16:23:14.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-20T16:24:23.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "33",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s02",
      "sequence_id": 34,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "So it doesn't matter which side we clear the x terms from first?",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s02-t034",
      "start_time": "2026-01-20T16:24:23.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-20T16:24:54.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "34",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s02",
      "sequence_id": 35,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Right, as long as you do the same operation to both sides, the path can vary.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s02-t035",
      "start_time": "2026-01-20T16:24:57.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-20T16:25:38.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "35",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s02",
      "sequence_id": 36,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "That makes sense because we're just keeping the equation balanced either way.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s02-t036",
      "start_time": "2026-01-20T16:25:40.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-20T16:26:05.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "36",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s02",
      "sequence_id": 37,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Exactly — balance is the whole principle behind every move we made.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s02-t037",
      "start_time": "2026-01-20T16:26:09.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-20T16:26:41.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "37",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s02",
      "sequence_id": 38,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "So the bracket expansion was really just applying distribution before anything else.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s02-t038",
      "start_time": "2026-01-20T16:26:46.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-20T16:27:14.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "38",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s02",
      "sequence_id": 39,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Right, and collecting the x terms is just combining like terms across the equals sign.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s02-t039",
      "start_time": "2026-01-20T16:27:21.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-20T16:27:44.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "39",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s02",
      "sequence_id": 40,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "So all of this really only used two ideas: distributing and combining like terms.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s02-t040",
      "start_time": "2026-01-20T16:27:52.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-20T16:28:31.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "40",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s02",
      "sequence_id": 41,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "That's the whole toolkit for this kind of equation, really.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s02-t041",
      "start_time": "2026-01-20T16:28:35.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-20T16:28:55.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "41",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s02",
      "sequence_id": 42,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "Let me plug x equals 8 back into the original to make sure it holds.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s02-t042",
      "start_time": "2026-01-20T16:28:56.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-20T16:29:55.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "42",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s02",
      "sequence_id": 43,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Go ahead, work out both sides with that value.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s02-t043",
      "start_time": "2026-01-20T16:29:59.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-20T16:30:43.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "43",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s02",
      "sequence_id": 44,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "Hmm, let me get the arithmetic straight in my head first.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s02-t044",
      "start_time": "2026-01-20T16:30:47.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-20T16:31:44.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "44",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s02",
      "sequence_id": 45,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Take your time with it.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s02-t045",
      "start_time": "2026-01-20T16:31:44.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-20T16:32:51.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "45",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s02",
      "sequence_id": 46,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "5 times 8 minus 3 is 5 times 5, which is 25.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s02-t046",
      "start_time": "2026-01-20T16:32:54.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-20T16:34:00.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "46",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s02",
      "sequence_id": 47,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "And the other side?",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s02-t047",
      "start_time": "2026-01-20T16:34:00.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-20T16:35:02.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "47",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s02",
      "sequence_id": 48,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "2 times 8 plus 9 is 16 plus 9, which is also 25 — it checks out.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s02-t048",
      "start_time": "2026-01-20T16:35:09.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-20T16:35:32.000Z"
    }
  ],
